  "source_scope_note": "The selected problem is Theorem 1.1 for the free positive-mass Klein--Gordon equation on Euclidean space, with a continuous nonnegative periodic damping satisfying the exact geometric-control condition. The exponential energy-decay constants are uniform under damping rescaling by eta>=1. The complete author body retains the parameter-controlled semigroup transfer, dissipativity, block-resolvent/scaling reduction, low-frequency observability and small-damping high-frequency contradiction. Standard named functional calculus, semigroup and semiclassical-calculus prerequisites remain explicit references; damping without geometric control and polynomial-decay conclusions are unselected context.",
